# Imported content is a BUILD PRODUCT, never committed.
#
# examples/langpop/import.p writes the files in this directory out of
# JMdict and KANJIDIC2, which are CC BY-SA 4.0 (EDRDG).  Share-alike on a
# dictionary is fine for a dictionary and poison for a tutor, so the
# imported content stays on upstream's layer: regenerated from upstream on
# demand, and not part of anything the project ships.
#
# What IS committed is the curation -- graph/ja/picks/*.pl, which entries
# at which level under which identity.  That part is ours.
#
# The directory itself is committed, because import.p writes into it and
# will not create it.
#
# Everything, and not *.pl: Poplog's syscreate keeps back versions of a
# file by suffixing the name with `-` (REF * SYSIO pop_file_versions), so
# a re-import used to leave an n5-words.pl- here that *.pl did not match.
# import.p turns that off now, but a build directory should not be able
# to offer anything for commit in the first place.
*
!.gitignore
